            "en": "Then comes the verb that gives the verse its character: yukawwiru al-layla 'ala an-nahar, He winds the night over the day, and the day over the night. The root k-w-r occurs in the Quran in only two places, twice in this verse and once at 81:1, where the sun itself is wound up. Al-Qurtubi gives the root sense. Takwir in the language, he says, is throwing a thing so that part of it lies upon part, as goods are piled on one another, and from it comes kawr al-'imama, the winding of a turban.",
